# =============================================================================
# TorProxyManager - per-instance torrc template
#
# This file is rendered once per Tor instance on every start. Edit it to tune
# Tor behaviour for ALL endpoints, then restart the proxies from the dashboard.
#
# Available placeholders (Go text/template syntax):
#   {{.InstanceID}}   1-based instance number
#   {{.SocksPort}}    first SOCKS5 port of this process's block
#   {{.SocksPorts}}   list of ALL SOCKS5 ports served by this process
#   {{.ControlPort}}  control port for this instance (control_port_start + n)
#   {{.BindAddress}}  loopback bind address (from bind_address)
#   {{.DataDir}}      private data directory for this instance (quoted)
#   {{.LogFile}}      per-instance notice log (quoted)
#   {{.GeoIPFile}}    GeoIP database found next to tor.exe (quoted, may be empty)
#   {{.GeoIPv6File}}  GeoIPv6 database found next to tor.exe (quoted, may be empty)
#
# REQUIRED lines (the manager depends on them): SocksPort, ControlPort,
# CookieAuthentication 1, DataDirectory, Log ... file {{.LogFile}}
# =============================================================================

# Instance {{.InstanceID}}  |  SOCKS {{.SocksPort}}  |  Control {{.ControlPort}}

# SOCKS5 listeners - loopback only. One tor process serves a whole block of
# ports; every port gets its own isolated circuits (and IsolateSOCKSAuth gives
# each SOCKS username/password its own circuit too).
{{range .SocksPorts}}SocksPort {{$.BindAddress}}:{{.}}
{{end}}

# Control port used for bootstrap monitoring, NEWNYM and graceful shutdown.
# Authenticated with a per-instance cookie file; never exposed off-host.
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:{{.ControlPort}}
CookieAuthentication 1

# Each instance MUST have its own data directory.
DataDirectory {{.DataDir}}

# Client-only operation: never relay or exit traffic for others.
ClientOnly 1
ExitRelay 0
PublishServerDescriptor 0

# Speed tuning for many parallel clients.
MaxClientCircuitsPending 128
CircuitBuildTimeout 40
CircuitStreamTimeout 30
NewCircuitPeriod 15
AvoidDiskWrites 1

# Scrub addresses from logs.
SafeLogging 1

# GeoIP databases (auto-detected from the Tor Expert Bundle / Tor Browser).
{{if .GeoIPFile}}GeoIPFile {{.GeoIPFile}}
{{end}}{{if .GeoIPv6File}}GeoIPv6File {{.GeoIPv6File}}
{{end}}
# --- Optional tuning (uncomment as needed) -----------------------------------
# Warn when an application sends a raw IP instead of a hostname (DNS leak hint).
# Use socks5h:// in your clients so DNS is resolved through Tor.
#WarnUnsafeSocks 1
#SafeSocks 1

# Rotate circuits more or less often (seconds, default 600).
#MaxCircuitDirtiness 600

# Restrict exits to specific countries (requires GeoIP files next to tor.exe).
#ExitNodes {us},{ca}
#StrictNodes 1

# Use bridges / pluggable transports (copy the lines from bridges.torproject.org).
#UseBridges 1
#ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec pluggable_transports\lyrebird.exe
#Bridge obfs4 ...

# Notice-level log, viewable per instance from the dashboard.
Log notice file {{.LogFile}}
